<p>Peru&#x27;s presidential and congressional election was still unresolved on April 13 after logistical failures in Lima kept thousands of people from voting, prompting authorities to grant a one-day extension for affected polling centers and delaying the national result. The first round featured 35 presidential contenders, underscoring the fragmentation of Peruvian politics after years of instability in which the country has cycled through eight presidents since 2018 and is now choosing what could become its ninth president in 10 years. Exit polls showed Keiko Fujimori of Popular Force leading with about 16% of the vote, far below the threshold for an outright victory, so a runoff looks likely; some reports pointed to Rafael López Aliaga of Popular Renewal as the probable second-place contender, though the final standings remained unclear because of the delayed count. The disrupted process added to public frustration and distrust, but the extension also gave tens of thousands of voters who were initially blocked from casting ballots another chance to take part.</p><img src='https://kagiproxy.com/img/-npy5navL_lbskto31-HgiXabRSWoDrhuo55FugSA-obp9VlNihAKPMjDif3tr0OuAmyN-RI-6piNIsmoOpxNDSNF3P4dEdoLfCxqOB7WPe6DGowZTK_m7CXjutXuAiX5Bb_VFs-sfTUo6PWechrbiccbV6Td2JoDVCnOE23x_KhQc5IWw' alt='People pass a banner with electoral information at a polling station in Lima on April 12, 2026.' /><br /><h3>Highlights:</h3><ul><li>Election scale: Voting began at 7 a.m. local time, with about 27 million people eligible to cast ballots at more than 10,000 polling centers nationwide.</li><li>Lima disruption: Authorities said 15 voting centers in Lima, containing 211 polling stations, could not be set up, leaving 63,300 voters unable to cast ballots on the original day.</li><li>Police searches: Police and prosecutors searched the electoral authority&#x27;s headquarters and a private company as they investigated delays in delivering voting materials.</li><li>Broader stakes: A likely runoff will extend uncertainty at a time of rising crime and intensifying competition between the United States and China for influence in Peru.</li></ul><blockquote>I have to work and I can’t vote. These elections are a disaster. - Margarita Sandoval</blockquote><h3>Perspectives:</h3><ul><li>Electoral authorities: Officials said 99.8% of polling stations were installed, framing the disruption as concentrated at a limited number of Lima sites rather than a nationwide breakdown. (<a href='https://en.mercopress.com/2026/04/12/peru-closes-a-troubled-election-day-and-begins-a-lengthy-count-with-outcome-uncertain'>MercoPress</a>)</li><li>Margarita Sandoval, voter: After waiting two hours outside her polling place in Chorrillos, she said she had to leave for work without casting a ballot. (<a href='https://michaelwest.com.au/peruvians-vote-in-crowded-presidential-race/'>Michael West</a>)</li></ul><h3>Sources:</h3><ul><li><a href='https://abcnews.com/International/wireStory/perus-voters-face-choice-35-contenders-ninth-president-131969914'>Peru&#x27;s voters face choice of 35 contenders for ninth president in 10 years</a> - abcnews.com</li><li><a href='https://www.lemonde.fr/en/international/article/2026/04/13/peru-exit-polls-show-fujimori-ahead-runoff-likely_6752352_4.html'>Peru exit polls show Fujimori ahead, runoff likely</a> - lemonde.fr</li><li><a href='https://www.straitstimes.com/world/fujimori-poised-for-peru-presidential-runoff-but-opponent-still-unclear'>Fujimori poised for Peru presidential runoff but opponent still unclear</a> - straitstimes.com</li><li><a href='https://michaelwest.com.au/peruvians-vote-in-crowded-presidential-race/'>Peruvians vote in crowded presidential race</a> - michaelwest.com.au</li><li><a href='https://www.nytimes.com/2026/04/12/world/americas/peru-presidential-election.html'>Peru Votes for President, With 35 Names on the Ballot</a> - nytimes.com</li><li><a href='https://www.dw.com/en/peru-general-elections-no-clear-frontrunner-runoff-likely/a-76756162'>Peru general elections: No clear frontrunner, runoff likely</a> - dw.com</li><li><a href='https://en.mercopress.com/2026/04/12/peru-closes-a-troubled-election-day-and-begins-a-lengthy-count-with-outcome-uncertain'>Peru closes a troubled election day and begins a lengthy count with outcome uncertain</a> - mercopress.com</li><li><a href='http://www.euronews.com/video/2026/04/13/peru-faces-protests-as-election-delays-fuel-doubts-over-vote-integrity'>Peru faces protests as election delays fuel doubts over vote integrity</a> - euronews.com</li><li><a href='https://www.scmp.com/news/world/americas/article/3349823/peru-extends-voting-president-and-congress-amid-delays-polling-sites'>Peru presidential run-off looms as Fujimori leads troubled vote</a> - scmp.com</li><li><a href='https://www.thehindu.com/news/international/peru-presidential-election-results-delayed-after-thousands-get-one-day-voting-extension/article70856092.ece'>Peru presidential election results delayed after thousands get one-day voting extension</a> - thehindu.com</li><li><a href='https://apnews.com/article/peru-presidential-election-crime-fujimori-aliaga-980a5ee78d1fed794dc6c9b90f9a1ce4'>Exit polls show Popular Force&#x27;s Keiko Fujimori leading the presidential election with about 16 percent of the vote, with no candidate securing a majority and a run-off expected between Fujimori and Popular Renewal&#x27;s Rafael López Aliaga.</a> - apnews.com</li><li><a href='https://www.freemalaysiatoday.com/category/world/2026/04/13/perus-police-investigators-raid-election-hq-amid-vote-delays'>Peruvian police and prosecutors conduct searches at the electoral authority&#x27;s headquarters and a private company as part of an investigation into delays in delivering voting materials that prevent more than 60,000 people from voting. Officials attribute the issue to logistical failures affecting multiple polling stations in Lima. The electoral authority later announces that some polling stations will reopen. (